 "answerVoice": "female",
 "notes": "Static camera; the rocket box follows the body upward and is off from 13.0 (only the flame trail stays). Tower and rocket touch in the picture: split along x = 0.40, so the tower's top arm that reaches over the rocket is outside the tower box. The smoke box is the main mass along the ground; the tall puff at the far left (8.5-12.5) is partly outside it because the tower box sits there. Before ignition (0-3.0) the smoke box is the white vapour cloud at the lower left. The launch mount under the rocket also stays in place but is not a separate target. 'concrete' = the pad surface in the foreground.",
